xperience Resumes, Cover Letters and Interviews Resumé Outlines Job Resources NWU Career Closet Plan for Grad School Employer Services Parents & Families Career Center Staff Menu Log in/Sign Up Career Assistance Network Follow us on Instagram Contact or visit us Career Center Roy G. Story Student Center, Lower Level 5000 Saint Paul Avenue Lincoln, NE 68504-2794 (402) 465-2224 career [at] nebrwesleyan.edu (career[at]nebrwesleyan[dot]edu) Hours Monday – Friday, 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. Drop-In Hours (academic year only) Resume/Cover Letter only Tuesdays, 1 - 3 p.m. Wednesdays, 10 a.m. - noon Thursdays, 3 - 5 p.m. Career Center Career Services for Students and Alumni The Career Center offers both in-person and virtual appointments. You can schedule appointments though Handshake (\"Career Center\" >> \"Appointments\"). We look forward to connecting with you! Questions? Reach out to us at career [at] nebrwesleyan.edu (career[at]nebrwesleyan[dot]edu) . Major and Career Exploration Explore Nebraska Wesleyan’s majors and minors offered. Also download \"What can I do with this degree?\" booklets. Gain Experience Internships are a great way for college students to build valuable work experience. In fact, some majors at NWU require them. Résumés, Cover Letters and Interviews The Career Center can help you write your résumés and cover letter, as well as prepare you for successful interviews. Job Resources Employers post full-time and part-time positions, internships, and volunteer/service opportunities on Handshake for you to review and apply for. Plan for Grad School Career Center coaches can help you prepare for graduate school entrance, find the right school for your area of interest, search for financial aid, and prepare your graduate school application. Need help scheduling an appointment? Check out this quick tutorial for more information. Connect with Nebraska Wesleyan alumni about their career paths using the Career Assistance Network! Check out this quick tutorial for more info